Report pipe_progress's read and write errors.
A read error on standard input ended the copy as if the input had
ended, and a failed write to standard output was ignored, losing that
block, while the copy went on. Either way nothing was reported and the
exit status was 0, so a broken copy looked like a good one. Exit with
an error message and status 1 on a write error, and on a read error
after the final newline.

---
 debianutils/pipe_progress.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/debianutils/pipe_progress.c
+++ b/debianutils/pipe_progress.c
@@ -42,10 +42,12 @@
 			t = new_time;
 			bb_putchar_stderr('.');
 		}
-		full_write(STDOUT_FILENO, buf, len);
+		xwrite(STDOUT_FILENO, buf, len);
 	}
 
 	bb_putchar_stderr('\n');
+	if (len < 0)
+		bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(bb_msg_read_error);
 
 	return 0;
 }
